1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:05,300
Could you trace this whole diagram in one continuous stroke?

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:09,600
Follow every line exactly once.

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,700
One line always remains at the end.

4
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:26,300
In 1999, two psychologists asked:

5
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,700
How well did you do, and how well do you think you did?

6
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:35,200
The lowest-scoring group actually outperformed about 12% of people;

7
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:39,500
yet believed they had outperformed about 62%.

8
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,500
Solving a problem takes knowledge.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,400
Spotting your own mistakes may take it too.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,700
Missing knowledge may also hide the mistake.

11
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:58,700
Back to this diagram: at a junction, one line in, one line out.

12
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:03,300
With three lines, one is always left unpaired.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,400
Such a junction must be a start or an end.

14
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:12,400
There are only two: a start and an end.

15
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,500
But this diagram has four such junctions.

16
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:20,200
So it cannot be traced under these rules.

17
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
What you learn also becomes a measure of your own judgment.

18
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:29,500
But do not rush to use it to label other people.

19
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:34,100
Grouping and measurement may also amplify the gap.

20
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:38,600
Later studies of intelligence did not all agree.

21
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:42,700
The size of the bias depends on the task and the method.

22
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,800
So, do not mistake familiarity for mastery.

23
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,000
Find a task and try it yourself.

24
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:57,500
Then let the result test your prediction.

25
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:02,600
Where the result differs from what you expected,

26
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:06,800
you have found what to learn next.
